Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Choi State Thermal Sweep -- Transfer-Tensor Method", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"eb7f7d8c-d86d-594e-a37d-99f6cdae0102"],

Cell["\<\
Computes chi(t) of the edge-spin dynamical map for a list of chain lengths  
LList and inverse temperatures betaList, with delta fixed. Uses the validated 
transfer-tensor construction (Method 2 of choi_methods_comparison.m) \
throughout -- 
the brute-force branch (Method 1 / ChoiChannelF) is not present in this file. \
   
                                                                              \
    
Key precomputation separation:                                                \
     
  Per (L, delta): Ha, {Eval, Evec}, Tmat, Ucols, dEflat -- built once.        \
    
  Per (L, delta, beta): rhoChain, KmatFast, choiFnFast -- built per beta.     \
     
                                                                              \
    
Output per (L, beta) run:                                                     \
     
  ChoiObservables_D<kk>_<betastr>.png  -- Purity and VNEntropy                \
    
  ChoiEigenvalues5_D<kk>_<betastr>.png -- first 5 eigenvalues of chi(t)       \
    
  choi_data_D<kk>_<betastr>.mx         -- full ChoiSeries result list         \
    
All files written to baseDir/L=<LL>/Choi/.                                    \
    \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"79afe4b4-abab-4848-bf5b-e31ff8c54403"],

